{
  "sn12.23:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.23 ",
  "sn12.23:0.2": "3. The Ten Powers ",
  "sn12.23:0.3": "Vital Conditions ",
  "sn12.23:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.23:1.2": "“Mendicants, I say that the ending of defilements is for one who knows and sees, not for one who does not know or see. ",
  "sn12.23:1.3": "For one who knows and sees what? ",
  "sn12.23:1.4": "‘Such is form, such is the origin of form, such is the disappearance of form. ",
  "sn12.23:1.5": "Such is feeling … ",
  "sn12.23:1.6": "Such is perception … ",
  "sn12.23:1.7": "Such are choices … ",
  "sn12.23:1.8": "Such is consciousness, such is the origin of consciousness, such is the disappearance of consciousness.’ ",
  "sn12.23:1.9": "The ending of the defilements is for one who knows and sees this. ",
  "sn12.23:2.1": "I say that this knowledge of ending has a vital condition, it doesn’t lack a vital condition. ",
  "sn12.23:2.2": "And what is it? ",
  "sn12.23:2.3": "You should say: ‘Freedom.’ ",
  "sn12.23:2.4": "I say that freedom has a vital condition, it doesn’t lack a vital condition. ",
  "sn12.23:2.5": "And what is it? ",
  "sn12.23:2.6": "You should say: ‘Dispassion.’ ",
  "sn12.23:2.7": "I say that dispassion has a vital condition. ",
  "sn12.23:2.8": "And what is it? ",
  "sn12.23:2.9": "You should say: ‘Disillusionment.’ ",
  "sn12.23:2.10": "I say that disillusionment has a vital condition. ",
  "sn12.23:2.11": "And what is it? ",
  "sn12.23:2.12": "You should say: ‘Truly knowing and seeing.’